import Text "mo:core/Text";

mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    let lines : [Text] = [
      "# IRL Backend API",
      "",
      "The IRL backend serves a one-page, Bangalore-focused directory plus a live web",
      "chat. It exposes three domains — chat, board (directory items), and user",
      "profiles — over Candid, and additionally exposes its structured data to the",
      "Caffeine Data Intelligence agent through `schema()` and `execute()`.",
      "",
      "All timestamps are `Nat` nanoseconds since the Unix epoch (`Time.now()`), not",
      "seconds or milliseconds. All identifiers are `Nat` counters starting at `0` and",
      "increasing by one per created record.",
      "",
      "## Authentication and identity",
      "",
      "- `postMessage`, `addItem`, and `saveCallerUserProfile` are update calls that",
      "  read the caller's principal. They do not reject anonymous callers, but an",
      "  anonymous caller is a distinct principal and its writes are attributed to it.",
      "- `getCallerUserProfile` and `getCallerEmail` are queries scoped to the caller's",
      "  own principal; they return `null` for a principal with no stored profile.",
      "- `listMessages` and `listItems` are public queries with no caller restriction.",
      "- The app's frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at",
      "  `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent already holding",
      "  the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app",
      "  principal against that origin (for example",
      "  `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the",
      "  user's full authority in this app until it expires.",
      "- Registration happens only when a caller signs in through the app's own",
      "  frontend. A principal that never did so is unregistered even when it belongs",
      "  to the app's owner, and a signed-in caller derived against a different origin",
      "  is a different principal than the one the frontend registered. Unregistered",
      "  callers can still read public queries and post; `getCallerUserProfile` and",
      "  `getCallerEmail` simply return `null` for them.",
      "",
      "## Chat",
      "",
      "### `listMessages : () -> query [Message]`",
      "",
      "Returns every message, sorted ascending by `id`. Public, no authentication.",
      "",
      "`Message` = `{ id : Nat; author : Principal; authorName : Text; text : Text; createdAt : Nat }`.",
      "",
      "- `author` is the posting caller's principal.",
      "- `authorName` is the poster's stored `displayName` at post time, or",
      "  `\"Anonymous\"` when the poster had no profile. It is a snapshot: later profile",
      "  edits do not change existing messages.",
      "- `createdAt` is nanoseconds since the Unix epoch.",
      "",
      "### `postMessage : (text : Text) -> async Message`",
      "",
      "Appends a message authored by the caller and returns the created `Message`.",
      "",
      "- The caller's current profile `displayName` is captured as `authorName`; if the",
      "  caller has no profile, `\"Anonymous\"` is used.",
      "- `text` is stored verbatim; the backend applies no length or content",
      "  validation.",
      "- Not idempotent: each call creates a new message with a fresh `id`. Retrying a",
      "  call that already succeeded creates a duplicate. There is no delete or edit",
      "  endpoint.",
      "",
      "## Board (directory items)",
      "",
      "### `listItems : () -> query [Item]`",
      "",
      "Returns every directory item, sorted ascending by `id`. Public, no",
      "authentication.",
      "",
      "`Item` = `{ id : Nat; title : Text; category : Category; area : Text; shortDescription : Text; fullDescription : Text; dateOrHours : ?Text; activityId : ?Text; startDate : ?Text; startTime : ?Text; endDate : ?Text; price : ?Text; ageRequirements : ?Text; address : ?Text; registrationLink : ?Text; mapsLink : ?Text; sourceLink : ?Text; lastVerified : ?Text; status : ?Text; tags : [Text]; createdBy : Principal; createdAt : Nat }`.",
      "",
      "`Category` is the variant `#events | #places | #food | #culture`.",
      "",
      "- `area` is free text (for example a Bangalore neighbourhood).",
      "- `activityId` is the spreadsheet activity ID (for example `\"CB001\"`).",
      "- `startDate`, `startTime`, and `endDate` are separate optional free-text",
      "  fields; `null` means unspecified.",
      "- `price`, `ageRequirements`, `address`, `registrationLink`, `mapsLink`,",
      "  `sourceLink`, `lastVerified`, and `status` are optional free text.",
      "- `tags` is an array of individual tag chips, not one comma-separated string.",
      "- `dateOrHours` is a legacy optional free-text field; new entries leave it",
      "  `null`.",
      "- `createdBy` is the adding caller's principal; `createdAt` is nanoseconds.",
      "",
      "The board ships pre-loaded with 20 seeded entries (activity IDs CB001–CB020)",
      "inserted once on first install. Seeding is idempotent: reloading or revisiting",
      "never duplicates them, and seeded entries are indistinguishable from added",
      "entries in the returned list.",
      "",
      "### `addItem : (title, category, area, shortDescription, fullDescription, dateOrHours, activityId, startDate, startTime, endDate, price, ageRequirements, address, registrationLink, mapsLink, sourceLink, lastVerified, status, tags) -> async Item`",
      "",
      "Adds a directory item created by the caller and returns it. Only `title`,",
      "`category`, `area`, and `shortDescription` are required; every other field is",
      "optional and may be `null` (or `[]` for `tags`). All text fields are stored",
      "verbatim with no validation.",
      "",
      "- Not idempotent: each call creates a new item with a fresh `id`. Retrying a",
      "  call that already succeeded creates a duplicate. There is no delete or edit",
      "  endpoint.",
      "",
      "## Profiles",
      "",
      "### `getCallerUserProfile : () -> query ?UserProfile`",
      "",
      "Returns the caller's stored profile, or `null` if none exists.",
      "",
      "`UserProfile` = `{ displayName : Text; verifiedEmail : ?Text }`.",
      "",
      "- `verifiedEmail` is populated from the caller's Internet Identity attributes",
      "  when available and is `null` otherwise.",
      "",
      "### `saveCallerUserProfile : (displayName : Text) -> async UserProfile`",
      "",
      "Sets the caller's `displayName` and returns the stored profile. The existing",
      "`verifiedEmail` is preserved; a caller with no profile gets `verifiedEmail =",
      "null`.",
      "",
      "- Idempotent in effect: calling it repeatedly with the same `displayName`",
      "  leaves the same profile. It never clears an existing `verifiedEmail`.",
      "",
      "### `getCallerEmail : () -> query ?Text`",
      "",
      "Returns the caller's verified email, or `null` when none is stored. This is the",
      "same value as `getCallerUserProfile().verifiedEmail`.",
      "",
      "## Authorization",
      "",
      "The backend includes the Caffeine authorization mixin, which provides",
      "role-based access control. The first caller to initialize access control",
      "receives the `#admin` role; subsequent callers receive the default role. Role",
      "assignment and admin checks are exposed by that mixin. The chat, board, and",
      "profile endpoints above do not themselves require a role.",
      "",
      "## Data Intelligence (`schema`, `execute`)",
      "",
      "`schema()` and `execute()` are provided by the OQL `Expose` mixin and let the",
      "Caffeine Data Intelligence agent query the backend's structured data in natural",
      "language. They are read-only and do not mutate state.",
      "",
      "## Errors and gotchas",
      "",
      "- No endpoint returns a `Result`; failures surface as traps. A trap rolls back",
      "  the whole call.",
      "- `listMessages` and `listItems` return the full collection with no pagination;",
      "  callers should expect the result to grow unbounded.",
      "- Timestamps are nanoseconds — divide by 1_000_000_000 for seconds.",
      "- `authorName` is a snapshot at post time, not a live join to the profile.",
      "- `postMessage` and `addItem` are not idempotent; a retried call duplicates.",
      "- Anonymous callers are valid principals and can post and add items.",
    ];
    lines.values().join("\n");
  };
};
